{"id": "73cc8c09-b84c-4788-9248-ccedde78a3d4", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The kmsKeyArn field only applies to fully managed knowledge bases, but this one uses VECTOR type with OSS as a custom vector store, so its absence doesn't mean the data is unencrypted — it's likely encrypted at rest with an AWS-owned key by default, making this a PASS or not applicable rather than a failure.

Actual encryption verification would need to look elsewhere: the OpenSearch Serverless encryption security policy (which is always encrypted, either AWS-owned or CMK), the data source's own serverSideEncryptionConfiguration for transient ingestion data, and the underlying S3 bucket's KMS settings. I shouldn't label this unencrypted — absence of the field is indeterminate for CMK usage, not evidence of no encryption at all.

"}]}
